The SR-IOV operator pod is not failing—it has never been scheduled because your only node is marked unschedulable.

What this tells us

Your cluster is an SNO (Single Node OpenShift) cluster.

Normally, the SR-IOV operator does the following:

1. Drain the node.


2. Apply SR-IOV configuration.


3. Reboot the node if required.


4. Uncordon the node.


5. Complete installation.



In your case, the process is stuck at:

CURRENT SYNC STATE = Draining

As a result:

Node is cordoned (SchedulingDisabled)

New operator pod cannot schedule

CSV remains Installing

NodeState remains InProgress


This is a circular dependency.

